1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:07,667
Real work in the middle: a worker, a site, a risk owner. Priora places agents around it.

2
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:16,133
WORKER (phone message): Hey, the bracket by the packing line has cracked again. We’re going to weld it before the night shift.

3
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:20,800
Priora hears the job, and asks for a photo.

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,000
Next, it summons only the specialists this site and job need.

5
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:36,433
Each checks its own conditions and reports back.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,400
When everything holds, the route opens. Work goes on, the record is kept, no one is disturbed.

7
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:56,367
One condition slips: the fire watch is half the policy. Priora brings it to the risk owner. Agents prepare, the human decides.

8
00:00:58,167 --> 00:01:00,367
Retain is never a default.

9
00:01:00,367 --> 00:01:04,300
Risk is kept on purpose, with its terms explicit.

10
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:10,867
Mitigate compares safeguards, and checks whether the work is back inside.

11
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:18,367
Transfer, simulated for now, asks outside capacity for terms and a price.

12
00:01:18,767 --> 00:01:21,400
Priora carries the case between rooms.

13
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,333
The risk owner stays in control.

14
00:01:27,867 --> 00:01:33,100
Priora turns physical work into explicit risk decisions, while the work happens.
